Hi Paula,

If you can get OUF/IOU models selected on that little data, and the uncertainties aren't too wild, then I don't see any issue.
If the model parameter uncertainties are large, you could consider expanding the window of the model fitting to be wider than that of the daily estimate.
If the models are some times too elliptical (because the data are by rare chance), then you can force isotropic=TRUE before model selection to only consider isotropic models.
Those are my experiences with working with tiny datasets.

Best,
Chris

